# GitHub-only agent workflow

Canonical repo: **https://github.com/Wyzird42/UV** (`origin`).

Cursor may label a Cloud Agent run **“PR #N”** in the UI. That is a run number, **not** the git branch name and **not** a GitHub Pull Request. Remote branches look like `cursor/<topic>` or `cursor/<topic>-<id>`.

## Do not (local repo)

- **Do not manage the user’s local git clone**: no `git checkout`, `git pull`, `git merge`, `git restore`, or “sync your machine” steps unless they explicitly ask.
- Do not tell them to run `pull.bat` or other local sync commands as part of handoff—they handle local themselves.
- Do not merge feature work into `main` and push `main`, unless they explicitly ask.
- Do not open GitHub Pull Requests unless they explicitly ask.

## Do (GitHub)

1. Base work on current **`origin/main`** (fetch is fine; avoid reshaping their local branch checkout).
2. Use branch names `cursor/<short-description>`.
3. Commit only related changes; never commit IDE artifacts (`.vs/`, `__vm/`, `*.vcxproj*`, etc.).
4. **Push the branch to GitHub:** `git push -u origin <branch>`.
5. Hand off with the **remote branch name** (and commit message if useful). Optionally link: `https://github.com/Wyzird42/UV/tree/<branch>`.

They merge to `main` on GitHub or locally when they choose.

## “Create branch and commit” actions

Branch + commit + push to GitHub when handoff is intended. **Do not push** when they say not to. Do not merge to `main` for them unless asked.
